Task 2: Share the Collection with Other Teams
Subtask 2.1: Build the Collection

    Navigate to the collection root directory:

cd ~/ansible-collections/mycompany/infrastructure

    Build the collection package:

ansible-galaxy collection build

This creates a tarball file like mycompany-infrastructure-1.0.0.tar.gz.

    Verify the build contents:

tar -tzf mycompany-infrastructure-1.0.0.tar.gz | head -20

Subtask 2.2: Test the Collection Locally

    Install the collection locally for testing:

ansible-galaxy collection install mycompany-infrastructure-1.0.0.tar.gz --force

    Verify installation:

ansible-galaxy collection list

    Test the collection with a simple playbook:

mkdir -p ~/test-collection
cd ~/test-collection
vim test-playbook.yml

---
- name: Test Custom Collection
  hosts: localhost
  connection: local
  gather_facts: yes
  
  tasks:
    - name: Display collection info
      debug:
        msg: "Testing mycompany.infrastructure collection"
    
    - name: Test webserver role (dry run)
      include_role:
        name: mycompany.infrastructure.webserver
      vars:
        company_name: "Test Company"
      check_mode: yes

    Run the test playbook:

ansible-playbook test-playbook.yml

